{"arrivo":"sv","origine":"la-new","origine_nome":"New Latin","livello2":"grc","livello2_nome":"Ancient Greek","n":8,"parole":[{"parola":"kamera","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"latinismo_dotto","incerta":"no","significato":"camera","termine_origine":"camera obscura","catena":[{"codice":"la-new","nome":"New Latin","termine":"camera obscura","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"καμάρα","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From New Latin camera obscura (literally “dark chamber”), because the first cameras used a pinhole and a dark room; from Latin camera (“chamber or bedchamber”), from Ancient Greek καμάρα (kamára, “anything with an arched cover, a covered carriage or boat, a vaulted chamber, a vault”). Doublet of kam"},{"parola":"narkotikum","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"latinismo_dotto","incerta":"no","significato":"a narcotic","termine_origine":"narcoticum","catena":[{"codice":"la-new","nome":"New Latin","termine":"narcoticum","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ναρκωτικός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From New Latin narcoticum (an ellipsis of remedium narcoticum), neuter of narcoticus, from Ancient Greek ναρκωτικός (narkōtikós). Doublet of narkotisk."},{"parola":"skräcködla","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"no","significato":"a dinosaur (animal belonging to the clade Dinosauria)","termine_origine":"dīnosaurus","catena":[{"codice":"la-new","nome":"New Latin","termine":"dīnosaurus","categoria":"calco"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"δεινός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From skräck (“horror, terror”) + ödla (“lizard”). Calque of New Latin dīnosaurus, from Ancient Greek δεινός (deinós, “terrible, awesome, mighty, fearfully great”) + σαῦρος (saûros, “lizard, reptile”)."},{"